"How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29251407505682-How-to-reset-your-Toniebox-2-to-factory-settings)\nciteturn781search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings ... The Toniebox 2 will begin the factory reset and guide you through the process.\n\n# How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings\n\nThink of a factory reset as your Toniebox 2 “fresh start button.” It wipes everything clean and takes your Toniebox 2 back to the way it was on day one. Because it’s such a big step, a factory reset should only be used as a last resort, after you’ve tried all other troubleshooting tips.\nWhen to use a factory reset\n- Something went wrong during the initial setup and your Toniebox 2 isn’t responding as expected.\n- You’d like to return your Toniebox 2 and remove it from your tonies® account.\n\nTo Factory Reset your Toniebox 2, follow these steps:\n1. Turn on your Toniebox 2 and wait until the light ring turns green.\n2. Make sure the Toniebox 2 is not plugged in.\n3. Turn the Toniebox 2 upside down and press and hold both ears for 5 seconds until you hear a sound signal.\n4. Turn it back over – the light ring will glow white.\n5. Press and hold the small ear. The Toniebox 2 will begin the factory reset and guide you through the process.\n6. Wait until the Toniebox 2 confirms that the reset is complete.\nYour Toniebox 2 is now reset and ready for a brand-new start.\nFor in app guideance to factory reset:\n1. Open the tonies® app and log in to your account.\n2. Go to “Mine” and select your Toniebox 2.\n3. Tap “Settings” (top right corner).\n4. Scroll to the bottom and select “Factory reset instructions.”--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I activate Live function on my Creative Tonie? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036519484562-How-do-I-activate-Live-function-on-my-Creative-Tonie)\nciteturn781search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; When Live function is activated on a Creative Tonie, that will make it so that every new story that is uploaded to that Creative Tonie is placed first in the tracklist and will be played first. ... To activate Live function, you can use either the tonies app or my.tonies.com.\n\n# How do I activate Live function on my Creative Tonie?\n\nWhen Live function is activated on a Creative Tonie, that will make it so that every new story that is uploaded to that Creative Tonie is placed first in the tracklist and will be played first. This is the easiest way to make sure you can automatically hear the newest stories that have been uploaded to the Creative Tonie. To activate Live function, you can use either the tonies app or my.tonies.com. \n\nHow to activate Live function on your Creative Tonie:\n\nUsing the tonies app\n\n  1. Open the tonies app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Collection__11_.jpg\n \n  2. Tap on the 'Creative Tonies' header.\nImage: CT_Header__8_.jpg\n \n  3. Tap on the picture of the Creative Tonie you want to edit.\nImage: Only_CT__3_.jpg\n \n  4. Scroll down to the bottom of the page and tap on 'Advanced settings'.\nImage: CT_Advanced__2_.jpg\n \n  5. Here you can tap the toggle to turn the Live function on.\nImage: CT_Live.jpg\n \n  6. Now, you will just need to sync the Toniebox 1 and Creative Tonie to make sure that they receive the news that changes have been made. To do this, remove any Tonies from the Toniebox 1 and turn on the Toniebox 1. Then, pinch one of the Tonieboxes ears for about three seconds until you hear a sound. The LED will begin flashing blue while your Toniebox 1 establishes a connection with your Wi-Fi. You can then place the Creative Tonie onto the Toniebox 1 when the LED turns solid green and the new changes will be confirmed. Now, any future content uploaded to the Creative Tonie will automatically be placed first in the tracklist and played first.\n\nUsing my.tonies.com\n\n  1. Login to your account at my.tonies.com and click the 'Creative Tonies' header.\nImage: deskreorderFAQ1.jpg\n \n  2. Click the picture of the Creative Tonie you would like to edit.\nImage: deskreorderFAQ2.jpg\n \n  3. Here, you can click the toggle to turn the Live function on.\nImage: liveFunctiondesk1.jpg\n \n  4. Once clicked, the toggle should turn green and say 'On'.\nImage: liveFunctiondesk2.jpg\n \n  5. To confirm the changes, scroll down on the page and click 'Save Changes'.\nImage: liveFunctiondesk3.jpg\n \n  6. Now, you will just need to sync the Toniebox 1 and Creative Tonie to make sure that they receive the news that changes have been made. To do this, remove any Tonies from the Toniebox 1 and turn on the Toniebox 1. Then, pinch one of the Tonieboxes ears for about three seconds until you hear a sound. The LED will begin flashing blue while your Toniebox 1 establishes a connection with your Wi-Fi. You can then place the Creative Tonie onto the Toniebox 1 when the LED turns solid green and the new changes will be confirmed. Now, any future content uploaded to the Creative Tonie will automatically be placed first in the tracklist and played first.\n\nIf you run into any trouble with the Live function, send us a message and help will be on the way!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhat exactly is the Creative Tonie live function? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036607282322-What-exactly-is-the-Creative-Tonie-live-function)\nciteturn781search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; If you would like to use your Creative Tonie as a friendly little messenger, sending its owner messages from you, we recommend activating the live function in the tonies app or the Toniecloud.\n\n# What exactly is the Creative Tonie live function?\n\nIf you would like to use your Creative Tonie as a friendly little messenger, sending its owner messages from you, we recommend activating the live function in the tonies app or the Toniecloud.\n\nThe live function ensures that the Creative Tonie always puts the last track added at the top of the tracklist. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I change the order of the content on my Creative Tonie? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036510512658-How-do-I-change-the-order-of-the-content-on-my-Creative-Tonie)\nciteturn781search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; For steps on how to activate this Live function, take a look at our other support article here: How do I activate Live function on my Creative Tonie? ... Open the tonies app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\n\n# How do I change the order of the content on my Creative Tonie?\n\nNeed to make sure that your stories are in the correct order? Not to worry, you can always manually change the order of the tracks on each Creative Tonie. To do this, you can use either the tonies app or my.tonies.com.\n\nYou also have the ability to activate 'Live function'. This will make it so that every new story that is uploaded to that Creative Tonie is automatically placed first in the tracklist. For steps on how to activate this Live function, take a look at our other support article here: How do I activate Live function on my Creative Tonie?\n\nHow to change the order of content on your Creative Tonie:\n\nUsing the tonies app\n\n  1. Open the tonies app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Collection__2_.jpg\n \n  2. Tap on the 'Creative Tonies' header.\nImage: CT_Header.jpg\n \n  3. Tap on the picture of the Creative Tonie you want to edit.\nImage: Only_CT.jpg\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nToniebox 2 – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/sections/29036371272594-Toniebox-2